{
  "slug": "artist:neophyte",
  "name": "Neophyte",
  "editorial_article": "Neophyte formed in 1992 in Rotterdam after Jeroen Streunding and Danny Greten met at a local party and began experimenting with tracks on an Amiga computer using Protracker software. Initially dismissed by DJ Paul Elstak as 'pure noise', the group eventually earned a contract with his Rotterdam Records label to release early EPs like The Three Amiga's and Noise Is The Message. The trio, which included Robin van Roon until his departure in 1995 for studies, frequently operated under aliases such as Bodylotion and Masters of Ceremony. Their influence on the gabber scene expanded significantly through the launch of their own imprint, Neophyte Records, which has housed artists like Evil Activities and Tha Playah. Their 2005 compilation 13 Jaar Terreur reached number 29 on the Dutch Album Top 100, marking a transition from their early underground roots to a decade of influence in hardcore techno. The group has integrated live elements into their performances, notably adding guitarist Jarno Butter to replace van Roon for live sets. Throughout their career, they have maintained a consistent presence in hardcore with anthems such as 'Always Hardcore' and 'Execute', alongside high-profile collaborations with artists like Angerfist and Promo.",
